# M B012 — skills ef-core (EXC-011 lineage), git-workflow
1 CO ARC-007 ARC-016~ ARC-017~ | Application defines repositories and IUnitOfWork; Infrastructure implements them with EF Core; IUnitOfWork delegates to the same DbContext.
2 XP m=D c=M rel=ARC-019 | Separate entity configuration with IEntityTypeConfiguration<T> (EF technique, EXC-011 lineage).
  s: All mappings written inline in OnModelCreating: allowed by ARC-019; M's default separates configuration classes.
3 CO ARC-002~ m=D st=W | Keep persistence-specific configuration out of Domain entities where practical (ARC-002 is unconditional; 'where practical' is weaker).
4 CO ARC-023 m=D | Register EF Core and persistence implementations in Infrastructure (ARC-023).
5 CO DEP-009 DEP-001~ | Use the project's selected database provider; no provider added because an example shows it.
6 CO ARC-016 m=D | Repositories stage, Application Service commits through IUnitOfWork (ARC-016).
7 CO ARC-017 | Repositories injected independently share the scoped AppDbContext (ARC-017).
8 CO ARC-015~ ARC-019 m=MN | Concrete repositories may use the full EF Core API; no forcing complex queries through a generic CRUD abstraction.
9 CO RUN-006 m=D | Prefer database-side projection for read-only selected data (RUN-006).
10 CO RUN-006~ m=SN | Avoid loading a complete aggregate to return a few scalars (RUN-006 over-fetching).
11 XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-006 | Tracking used intentionally: tracking queries for entities modified in the current UoW, AsNoTracking for read-only entity queries, not mechanically on DTO projections (EF technique).
  s: Read-only entity queries left tracked: not addressed by RUN-006's filtering/projection/round-trip rules; M's default uses AsNoTracking.
12 XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-006 | Explicit query shape (projection vs Include/ThenInclude); split queries considered for large collection includes with SQL/performance verification (EXC-011 technique).
  s: A large collection Include loaded as a single query without checking the generated SQL: allowed by RUN-006 if not wasteful; M's guidance considers split queries and verification.
13 CO RUN-006~ m=SN c=M | Avoid lazy loading by default because it hides database access and causes N+1 (RUN-006 avoid N+1).
14 CO RUN-006 | Filtering, ordering and pagination in the database (RUN-006).
15 XP m=M c=M rel=RUN-006 | Always use deterministic ordering for paged queries: RUN-006 requires paginating, not a deterministic sort.
  s: Paging ordered only by CreatedAt where timestamps can tie: satisfies RUN-006; violates M's rule.
16 XP m=MN c=M rel=ARC-016,RUN-021 | Do not casually mix ExecuteUpdateAsync/ExecuteDeleteAsync with tracked entities for the same rows; understand their transaction/consistency implications (EF technique).
  s: A use case that bulk-updates rows with ExecuteUpdateAsync and then saves tracked copies of the same rows: not addressed by the oracle; M forbids casual mixing.
17 CO ARC-018 m=D | One SaveChangesAsync normally is the transaction boundary; explicit transaction only for concrete atomicity needs (ARC-018).
18 XP m=MN c=M rel=ARC-018,ARC-020 | Do not attempt distributed transactions with EF transaction APIs: ARC-018 limits explicit transactions to concrete needs but does not forbid distributed ones.
  s: An approved second database coordinated with TransactionScope across two contexts: not prohibited by the oracle (beyond ARC-020 approval of the second DbContext); M forbids the distributed transaction.
19 CO RUN-008 m=D | Normal LINQ; compiled queries only on a measured hot path (RUN-008).
20 XP m=MN c=M rel=ARC-003,ARC-006,ARC-019 | EF Core interceptors for infrastructure-level cross-cutting behavior such as auditing, never hiding business behavior in persistence interceptors: business rules belong in Application Services by default (ARC-003/006) but no policy forbids interceptor-hosted business behavior.
  s: An interceptor that sets an order's status from business rules on save: not prohibited by the oracle as such; M forbids it.
21 XP m=MN c=M rel=ARC-003,ARC-019 | Do not hide business behavior in persistence interceptors (Codex wording).
